 description: "Presentation skill for Codex, ChatGPT agents, and OpenAI-style agents that build, edit, verify, or iterate polished PowerPoint `.pptx` presentations, slides, and slide decks from structured `outline.json` or saved workspaces. Use for editable deck generation, lab/clinical/scientific deck assembly, investor or board decks, editorial briefs, presentation design, source-backed assets, optional generated-image slides, alignment QA, overflow/overlap checks, layout validation, and reusable deck workspaces. Aliases: `powerpoint-deck-builder`, `pptx-skill`, PowerPoint skill, PPTX skill, slide-deck generator, slides generator, deck builder, presentation generator."
 ---
 
+## dasCowork Runtime distribution policy
+
+This Runtime-owned distribution is restricted to creating a **new** PPTX, its
+automated QA receipt, and a workspace preview. It never opens, edits, rebuilds,
+or round-trips an existing PPTX. The packaged plugin contains only the audited
+allowlist required for that path; repository scripts for editing, web asset
+collection, or model-backed image generation are omitted.
+
+Before running a deck command, call `load_workspace_dependencies` and use only
+the returned Runtime Node, Python, module, native-binary, and font paths. Do
+not run `npm`, `npx`, `pip`, `uv`, `conda`, a bootstrap/setup script, or create a
+virtual environment. Do not discover or invoke a system Node, Python,
+LibreOffice, Poppler, font, or package manager.
+
+Images come from the application-host image-generation handoff or an already
+supplied workspace image. Never call a model HTTP endpoint, read a model API
+key, download an image, scrape a URL, or make another network request. Run the
+locked Runtime script through the ordinary app-server command path, so sandbox
+and approval rules continue to apply; do not add a PPT-specific Main-process
+tool or second execution service.
+
+The Runtime excludes React icon slugs (for example `fa6:`) and the
+React/sharp-dependent icon renderer. Use simple shapes, text, charts, tables,
+or approved workspace images instead.
+
